    "site_admin": false
  },
  "body": "Concurrent CLI and TUI readers could reject one another with AUTH_BUSY because every credential load took an exclusive lock. An auth status request also held that lock while waiting for the daemon.\n\nRead-only consumers now load credentials under a short shared lock and release it before HTTP. The shared guard cannot escape as a writable store. Login, revocation, forgetting credentials and journal writes retain exclusive custody; active writers still produce AUTH_BUSY. Directory identity is checked around successful loads, and existing ownership, permissions, symlink, hardlink, schema and size checks remain in force.\n\nThree regressions cover six overlapping readers, writer exclusion and displaced state, and an actual status request waiting on a withheld HTTP response. The measured inventory is 1,292 total / 1,246 standalone; removing the three new identities reproduces both previous inventory hashes exactly. No tests were removed or reclassified.\n\nValidation: focused CLI tests and strict Clippy passed. Full clean-commit required run passed: 1,246 standalone tests, 34 offline contract tests, lint/meta checks, security, generated-contract drift, rustdoc and documentation links. Simultaneous Tuiwright qualification on xbabe2 remains separate; this change does not claim native-provider or installation readiness.\n",
  "created_at": "2026-09-10T15:46:55Z",
